        "original_id": "fc1d4537-891f-5851-a92e-7464ee50c75b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Gaillardia, Browningia, Helenium\n- Taxa: Asteraceae, Helenieae, genera, cacti, flowering plants\n\nFacts:\n- Gaillardia, commonly called blanket flower, is a genus of flowering plants in the sunflower family Asteraceae that is native to North and South America.\n- Browningia is a genus of cacti with 11 accepted species and 3 unresolved species.\n- Helenieae is a tribe whose type genus is Helenium.\n- Gaillardia is among the best known members of the tribe Helenieae.",
